    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` and wrote the test suite in `tests/test_solution.py`. All 20 tests pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\n- **Validation:** bad `limit`, `window_seconds` or `cost` raise `ValueError`, and `bool` is rejected.\n- **Budget:** each client keeps its own list of `(time, cost)` entries, and an entry stops counting once it is exactly `window_seconds` old. Rejected requests are never recorded.\n- **`retry_after`:** it expires the client's oldest entries in order until the cost fits, then returns the time until that point.\n- **Time:** a `now` earlier than the latest one seen for any client raises `ValueError`.\n\nOne odd line remains in the suite. The last assertion in `test_retry_after` is a placeholder that always passes (`assert r.retry_after(\"a\", 10) == 2.0 - 0 if False else True`), so it checks nothing.",
